.TH BUILD-CV 1 "2026-09-17" "LatexCV" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
build-cv \- fetch, checkout and compile a CV branch to PDF
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B build-cv
.I branch-name
.RI [ path/to/file.tex ]
.RB [ --ats ]
.br
.B build-cv
.RB { --list | -l }
.br
.B build-cv
.RB { --help | -h }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B build-cv
automates the full local workflow for this repository's per-application
CV branches. It fetches from
.I origin ,
checks out
.I branch-name
(creating a local branch tracking
.I origin/branch-name
if one doesn't already exist locally), auto-detects which
.B CV-*.tex
file is new on that branch compared to
.IR main ,
compiles it with
.BR latexmk (1),
and opens the resulting PDF with
.BR open (1)
on macOS.
.PP
The script refuses to switch branches while the working tree has
uncommitted changes, to avoid losing local edits.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I branch-name
The branch to build, e.g.
.IR claude/signaltekniker-professionals-nord .
.TP
.RI [ path/to/file.tex ]
Optional. Skip auto-detection and compile this file explicitly (path
relative to the repository root). Needed when a branch touches more
than one
.B CV-*.tex
file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --ats
In addition to the normal PDF, also compile an ATS-friendly variant of
the CV: no photo, no framebox around it, plain header. This avoids the
most common reason automated resume-screening systems (Applicant
Tracking Systems) fail to parse a CV correctly. The output is named
.IB CV-name -ATS.pdf
next to the normal PDF in the same
.B build/
directory.
.IP
This requires the target
.B .tex
file to declare
.B \e providecommand{\e ATSMODE}{0}
near the top of its preamble (true for CVs built from 2026-09 onward;
older templates in this repo predate this convention and don't support
it -- the script will report a compile failure and point at the log if
so).
.TP
.BR --list ", " -l
List all local and remote (origin) branches, then exit. Does not touch
the working tree.
.TP
.BR --help ", " -h
Show a usage summary and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
List available branches:
.B build-cv --list
.TP
Build a specific application's CV and open it:
.B build-cv claude/signaltekniker-professionals-nord
.TP
Also produce an ATS-friendly variant:
.B build-cv claude/kronofogden-service-delivery-incident-problem-manager --ats
.TP
Disambiguate when a branch has more than one CV file:
.B build-cv claude/ils-ingenjor-academic-work roles_CVs/1.Primary_Roles/Foo/CV-Foo.tex
.SH FILES
.TP
.B sh/build-cv.sh
The script itself.
.TP
.B README.md
Local LaTeX installation instructions (macOS: MacTeX/BasicTeX via Homebrew).
.SH INSTALLING THIS MAN PAGE
This file can be read directly without installing it:
.PP
.RS
.B man ./sh/build-cv.1
.RE
.PP
To make
.B man build-cv
work from any directory, add the
.B sh/
directory to your
.B MANPATH
(it contains this file named as a section-1 page):
.PP
.RS
.B echo 'export MANPATH="$HOME/path/to/LatexCV/sh:$MANPATH"' >> ~/.zshrc
.br
.B source ~/.zshrc
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR latexmk (1),
.BR pdflatex (1)
